  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1957 0 R
  /Alt (Five panels plotting perfect recovery against sample size. With three misfitting items at rho 0.15 and 0.50, the S-X2 bootstrap climbs to about 93 percent at n = 1000 or 2000 while infit with Westfall-Young falls towards zero at n = 2000. At rho = 0.75 infit is higher than the S-X2 bootstrap at every n. With one misfitting item both methods are high from n = 500, and the S-X2 bootstrap is higher at n = 2000 for rho = 0.50.)
