2055 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 2054 0 R
  /Alt (Five panels plotting the share of datasets with a falsely flagged fitting item against sample size. With three misfitting items, infit with Westfall-Young rises steeply with n, reaching 87 to 100 percent at n = 2000 for rho 0.15 and 0.50, while the S-X2 bootstrap stays below 10 percent except at rho = 0.15 and n = 2000, where it reaches about 48 percent. With one misfitting item all methods except RMSEA stay low. RMSEA above .05 is near 100 percent at n = 150 in every panel.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 3241 0 R
>>
endobj

